.nh
.TH "PB-CONNECT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-connect - Create and attach to an environment terminal session


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb connect  [new] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and attach to an environment terminal session

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	show the pb versions used by this terminal session

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for connect

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	name for the fresh terminal session

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	attach an existing terminal session by name or ID

.PP
\fB--status-bar\fP=""
	status bar for this attach: auto, on, or off

.PP
\fB--status-bar-fullscreen\fP=""
	status bar in full-screen applications: hide or show

.PP
\fB--status-bar-theme\fP=""
	status bar theme: terminal, dark, light, or mono

.PP
\fB--transport\fP=""
	peer transport: a (auto), d (direct QUIC), q (relay QUIC), w (relay WSS), or r (relay race)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
